<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Product Requirements Document (PRD) – &lt;Product name&gt;</title>
<style>body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.45}h1{font-size:22pt;color:#2E3192}h2{font-size:14pt;color:#2E3192;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc}table{border-collapse:collapse}td{border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 10px}</style></head>
<body><h1>Product Requirements Document (PRD) – &lt;Product name&gt;</h1><p>Replace the grey guidance under each heading with your content.</p><table><tr><td>Document owner</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Version / status</td><td>v0.1 · Draft</td></tr><tr><td>Reviewers / approvers</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Last updated</td><td></td></tr></table>
<h2>1. Overview</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Product name, owner, status, last updated, one-line summary and links (designs, research, tickets).</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>2. Problem statement</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Who has the problem, how often, how painful, evidence (data, interviews), why now.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>3. Goals and non-goals</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Business and user goals with targets; what you will NOT do in this release.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>4. Users and personas</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>2–3 personas with context, goals and pain points; jobs-to-be-done.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>5. User journeys and stories</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Key flows and user stories with priority (P0/P1/P2) and acceptance criteria.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>6. Requirements</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Functional requirements (ID, description, priority, acceptance criteria) and non-functional (performance, security, privacy, accessibility).</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>7. Design and UX</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Wireframes or Figma links, key screens, edge cases, empty and error states.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>8. AI / data (if any)</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Model or rules, data needed, evaluation, guardrails, human fallback, cost per request.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>9. Success metrics</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>North Star, input metrics, guardrail metrics with baseline and target.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>10. Launch plan</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>MVP scope, phases, experiment design, rollout %, marketing and support readiness.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>11. Risks and dependencies</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Technical, legal, operational risks with mitigations; teams and vendors you depend on.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>12. Open questions and timeline</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Decisions still needed, owners, dates; milestones.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style="color:#888;font-size:9pt">Template from SkillNavora · skillnavora.in · Write it faster with the free AI writer: skillnavora.in/prd-writer</p></body></html>